QA Validation – LSR V4 Security Fixes Deployed
Hi Team,
The LSR V4 security fixes have been deployed to the QA environment.
The changes primarily impact User Management, access request/approval flows, notification emails, Excel export, and application error handling. There are no intended changes to the normal business functionality.
Key Functionalities / Validations
User Access Request & Approval
Validate Request User Access and My Approvals flows with valid requests.
Verify requester, security-group and request details remain correct, including when multiple requests are submitted concurrently.
Verify that request data is not shared or overwritten between users.
Approval Notification Email
Submit an access request containing HTML/script-related content in the applicable user-input field.
Verify the content in the approval notification is displayed as encoded/plain text and is not rendered or executed as HTML/script.
Verify normal notification content and formatting continue to work.
Excel Export / Overview
Verify Excel export continues to work correctly for valid requests.
Validate the affected error scenario and confirm that stack traces, Java class/method names, source-code line numbers, file paths, or other internal application details are not exposed to the user.
Verify normal Overview functionality is unaffected.
Add New User / Error Handling
Validate the Add New User flow for valid requests.
For an error/invalid request, verify that a controlled validation/error message is displayed (e.g., “Unable to add user, contact support”).
Verify that JDBC/Hibernate exception details, nested exceptions, SQL/database information, stack traces, or other internal implementation details are not exposed.
Regression Validation
Please verify that the following continue to work as expected:
Request User Access
My Approvals / Accept / Reject
User Management functionality
Approval notification emails
Add New User
Overview
Excel Export
Please share the validation results and any functional regression observed during QA testing.
Thanks,
